      "note": "PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, reconciliation of independent Tibetan-first and English-first proposals. The verse is translation. ri/mountains, nag po/dark, dus/time, rin chen/jewels and shing/trees record overt lexical exponents only. They do not assert that dark modifies mountains in Tibetan or that rin chen shing coordinates two objects: ILL:2684 instead reads days of darkness and trees made of jewel. The single like is assigned to final bzhin; initial dper shares the comparison frame and is omitted. The first world is the verse occurrence, worlds the second source occurrence; the two-world bracketed explanation is supplied apparatus and remains unwrapped. thun mong/collective and las/karma remain separate atoms in the relative-clause recast; supplied that is remains unwrapped. HGM yin min owns or not, with min/not inside it. HGM sems tsam licenses both complete school names, with sems/Mind inside each. The final snod kyi 'jig rten owns the established world where beings live. med pa min no is a distributed double negation: no independent denies or existence predicate is banked, and the full explanatory English sentence is not captured. No null is used for uncertainty or distributed meaning."
